@startuml 06-grading-task-state
' =====================================================================
' grading_task.ai_status lifecycle
' Traces to: FR-18, FR-29, FR-30, FR-42, NFR-6
'
' The unit with a lifecycle is the (submission x grading target) pair,
' not the submission, because the autograder marks individual targets
' as needing AI grading.
'
' Both modes share this machine. The only difference is WHO advances
' PENDING -> IN_PROGRESS: the same autograder run in immediate mode,
' a later triggered rerun in nightly mode.
' =====================================================================

title grading_task.ai_status

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica

[*] --> PENDING : autograder records test outcomes\nand creates a task for each target\nwith needs_ai_grading = true

PENDING : Functional test outcomes exist.
PENDING : AI grading not yet done.
PENDING : **This is the work queue.**

PENDING --> IN_PROGRESS : IMMEDIATE mode:\nsame autograder run\nclaims it at once
PENDING --> IN_PROGRESS : NIGHTLY mode:\na triggered rerun\nclaims it later

IN_PROGRESS : Claimed by one AI component.
IN_PROGRESS : claimed_at is set.

IN_PROGRESS --> COMPLETE : feedback rows written,\none marked is_selected
IN_PROGRESS --> FAILED : LLM or API error\nafter retries
IN_PROGRESS --> PENDING : claim timed out\n(container died mid-run)

COMPLETE : Feedback is in the database and
COMPLETE : has been written to results.json.
COMPLETE : Subsequent reruns SKIP this task.

COMPLETE --> [*]

FAILED : attempt_count incremented.
FAILED : last_error recorded.

FAILED --> PENDING : next nightly run,\nattempt_count < 3
FAILED --> ABANDONED : attempt_count >= 3

ABANDONED : Surfaced on the instructor dashboard
ABANDONED : for manual handling. Never retried
ABANDONED : automatically.

ABANDONED --> [*]

' Instructor-driven re-grade, e.g. after a rubric fix
COMPLETE --> PENDING : instructor requests\nre-grade of this target
ABANDONED --> PENDING : instructor requests\nretry

note right of PENDING #FFF8DC
  **Claiming must be atomic.**
  A bulk "Rerun Autograder" starts many
  containers at once, and a retried night can
  overlap a slow previous one. Claim by
  transitioning, in one conditional UPDATE:

  UPDATE grading_task
     SET ai_status = 'IN_PROGRESS',
         claimed_at = now()
   WHERE id = :id
     AND ai_status = 'PENDING'

  Zero rows updated means someone else has it.
  Skip. A read-then-write version will double
  bill.
end note

note as N2 #FFF8DC
  **Why COMPLETE must be sticky**
  Gradescope's rerun is a bulk action over the
  whole assignment, so every nightly trigger
  re-executes the container for every submission
  ever made, including ones graded weeks ago.

  If COMPLETE tasks were re-queued, cost would
  grow with the square of the term. The skip
  branch in 04-sequence-nightly.puml is not an
  optimisation, it is load-bearing.
end note

note as N3 #FFF8DC
  **IN_PROGRESS needs a timeout, OQ-5**
  If a container is killed between claim and
  write, the task sits in IN_PROGRESS forever
  and no later run will pick it up, because
  claiming only matches PENDING.

  Simplest fix: a task in IN_PROGRESS with
  claimed_at older than the autograder timeout
  is treated as PENDING. Whoever implements
  claiming owns this.
end note

@enduml
